  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Expect on and off showers through Saturday. \nRainfall totals will be light, so the day wont be a complete \nwashout.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nSurface low pressure is slowly drifting near Nova Scotia this\nafternoon, with a trof extending back across the CWA, while an \nupper low is moving SE across the region. Showers will persist \nacross the region rest of today, with the better chances across\nnorthern 2/3rd of the CWA. Could also have the slight chance of\nan afternoon thunderstorm. The surface/upper lows vertically \nstack across the Maritimes tonight into Saturday, slowing the \nmovement of the system. A disturbance moving around the \nMaritimes system will rotate across the region Saturday. Shower \nchances will persist tonight into Saturday but mostly isolated \nat night.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Rain chances remain limited through midweek, \naccompanied by near to below normal temperatures. The next best \nchance for precipitation arrives Wednesday night into Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nNorth Atlantic blocking weakens Sunday evening allowing for the\nstacked low track NE. Expecting dry conditions between Sunday\ninto Tuesday with temperatures near or slightly below normal.\nHighs in the 70s with lows in the 40s but potentially some upper\n30s in the cold spots across Northern Maine on Monday AM. A weak\ncold front crosses the region Tuesday AM into Tuesday PM with\nisolated to scattered rain showers. Wednesday night into\nThursday much of the global ensembles are pointing to a more\nrobust 500mb shortwave in the northern stream to provide another\nchance of widespread rain showers. Significant uncertainty on\ntiming and how much rainfall we will end up with given the\ndifferences between showers and stratiform precip.",
